meta {
  name: Invite to the active account
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{bffUrl}}/invites
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "pessoa@empresa.com",
    "role": "developer",
    "grants": []
  }
}

docs {
  It requires the owner or admin role in the active account.

  **The invite has NO token.** The `id` in the response is what the e-mail's link
  carries, and it grants nothing on its own: acceptance requires the VERIFIED
  e-mail of whoever is signed in to be the invite's. That is what allowed the id to
  travel in plain text in the event, in the timeline and in the e-mail — before, a
  bearer token turned any log read into a valid invite.

  `grants` goes up empty on purpose: a resource grant has no default (ADR-0009).
  Whoever invites decides what to share, explicitly.
}
